=== printed ===

 rebuild whenever the source changes, and keep the server up


Rebuilding whenever the source changes start watch respawning on exit $ just watch
Keeping the server up start serve respawning on exit $ python3 -m http.server 8080

Both are running and will come back whenever they exit.


 🤖 Job watch exited: complete after 8s, run 1, respawned.

    go build ./...
    built in 3s

 🤖 Job watch exited: failed after 8s, exit(1), run 2, respawned.

    go build ./...
    cmd/oh/draw.go:41:9: undefined: getWidth

 🤖 Job watch exited: complete after 8s with no output, run 3, respawned.
 🤖 Job serve exited: failed after 0s with no output, run 2, the job could not be respawned: no
    namespaces left.
 🤖 Job lint exited: failed after 0s, exit(127), run 4, not respawned after 3 runs in a row each
    ended within 2s.

    bash: golangci-lint: command not found



 wait for the next rebuild, stop it, then bring lint back


job wait watch Waiting for the next rebuild 3L
stop watch (Rebuilding whenever the source changes)
Bringing lint back restart lint respawning on exit

The rebuild passed, the watcher is stopped, and lint is respawning again.
